%% alt: A line chart of the average queueing wait for one busy server, in multiples of the time one request takes to serve. It rises slowly at first, then steeply: about 0.4 at 30% busy, 1 at 50%, 2.3 at 70%, 4 at 80%, 9 at 90% and 19 at 95%.
%% caption: Past about 80% busy, a little more load means a lot more waiting. That is why capacity plans target 60–70%.
xychart-beta
  title "Waiting time explodes as a server nears 100% busy"
  x-axis "Utilisation (%)" [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90, 95]
  y-axis "Average wait (× service time)" 0 --> 20
  line [0.11, 0.25, 0.43, 0.67, 1.0, 1.5, 2.33, 4.0, 9.0, 19.0]
